    {
      "id": 161,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -1798.8912343293975,
        5218.737208028643
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        150
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "H3 Studio x SelfLift. The Guide node hands its positive conditioning and its target latent to the SelfLift draft sampler, and its v2v_denoise output still drives H3 Basic Scheduler's denoise socket -- that is what makes the restyle amount work here. The decoders hang off the save node, so the draft mode keeps the latent to itself and nothing downstream runs. The TST node is optional: delete it for the plain run. TST and the sampler's high-resolution tiling cannot run together; the sampler refuses that combination rather than silently skipping the correction. The Turbo LoRA of H3 Studio's own example is not in this graph: it comes from the separate ComfyUI-MiniMax-H3-Turbo pack, and the model goes straight to the sampler without it."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "CLICK HERE TO THE RIGHT TO OPEN THE EDITOR ---->"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
